   "install": {
    "title": "Installing Subtitle Edit on macOS",
    "html": "<p>As of <strong>v5.2.0</strong>, the <code>.dmg</code> is signed with an Apple Developer ID and notarized by Apple, so it opens normally — no Terminal quarantine-removal step is needed:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Download</strong> and <strong>double-click</strong> the <code>.dmg</code> file to mount it.</li>\n<li>In the window that appears, <strong>drag <code>Subtitle Edit.app</code> into your <code>Applications</code> folder</strong>.</li>\n<li>Open <strong>Subtitle Edit</strong> from Applications (or Launchpad).</li>\n</ol>",
    "truncated": false,
